From c8492df8f98c4ffd9a7f205b12fbd509e6671cea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "5455945@gmail.com" <5455945@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:21:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] tools: add a minimal Chrome Sync backend for bookmarks

Serve Chromium's sync endpoint at POST .../command/ on the same origin as
the Gaia-compatible login service, so a client that signs in to the local
account can also sync bookmarks.

Protocol details follow the tree:
  * /command/ path and gzip request bodies
    (components/sync/engine/sync_manager_impl.cc,
     components/sync/engine/net/http_bridge.cc)
  * ClientToServerMessage / ClientToServerResponse / SyncEntity
    (components/sync/protocol/sync.proto, sync_entity.proto)
  * permanent bookmark folders and server ids
    (components/sync/engine/loopback_server/)

Implementation:
  * src/pb.mjs: dependency-free protobuf wire codec (incl. proto2 groups)
  * src/sync-store.mjs: per-account store, monotonic versions, permanent
    entities, clear-on-demand
  * src/sync.mjs: GetUpdates, Commit, ClearServerData, /event
  * EntitySpecifics are stored opaquely, so bookmarks (and unencrypted
    other datatypes) round-trip without server-side schema knowledge
  * persistent 16-byte keystore key returned in encryption_keys
  * gaia-config now contains sync_url; --sync-url also works
  * optional TLS (--tls-cert/--tls-key) for hosts-mapping deployments

Tests: 10 new end-to-end sync tests (27 total).
